<article class="env-lemma" id="0BR9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BR9">Lemma <span data-tag="0BR9">10.46.6</span>.</a> Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. Let $p$ be a prime number. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$k'$ is generated as a field extension of $k$ by elements $x$ such that there exists an $n > 0$ with $x^{p^ n} \in k$ and $p^ nx \in k$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$k = k'$ or the characteristic of $k$ and $k'$ is $p$ and $k'/k$ is purely inseparable. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x \in k'$. If there exists an $n > 0$ with $x^{p^ n} \in k$ and $p^ nx \in k$ and if the characteristic is not $p$, then $x \in k$. If the characteristic is $p$, then we find $x^{p^ n} \in k$ and hence $x$ is purely inseparable over $k$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>